1
00:00:01,480 --> 00:00:02,310
Hello there!

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:07,897
This definitely looks like the
Labyrinth Stratum's Transfer Circle.

3
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:08,810
Well, dammit!

4
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:12,197
I bet Kerrioll tampered with the
Origin Stratum's Transfer Circle,

5
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,917
which I should have known he would do.

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,237
So, what you're telling me is
that we've lost control over it.

7
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:18,150
That's right.

8
00:00:18,233 --> 00:00:19,637
But I don't think all is lost.

9
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:22,597
I seriously doubt his side
knows who got sent where.

10
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,257
The Transfer Circle doesn't have enough

11
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:26,397
power to return us to
Clearflow Lake Stratum,

12
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:27,437
I do know that much.

13
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:30,991
We'll need a magic stone that's
been charged up with power.

14
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:34,137
Then the Hunters Association
is the best place to start.

15
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:35,050
I agree.

16
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:50,200
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box.

17
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:52,617
But inside, I've still got a human soul.

18
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:53,897
In this new world of wonders,

19
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:57,537
I travel to and fro on the back
of my super strong partner, Lamas.

20
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:59,900
The name's Boxxo. Hello there.

21
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:01,880
That means yes, by the way.

22
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:59,580
That's right, surely!

23
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:30,577
to running out of preserved food, so
Boxo's arrival is quite the boon to us.

24
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:31,500
Thank you all.

25
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:35,357
The Labyrinth Stratum was struggling
with its own monster assault.

26
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:39,177
There are actual vending machines that
don't charge during times of disaster

27
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:42,677
so I tried taking a page from
their book by vending for free.

28
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:46,497
Director Labyrinth, have you
noticed any strangeness here lately?

29
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:50,137
You're referring to the wonkiness
with the transfer circle, I assume.

30
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:51,400
Well, not only that.

31
00:02:51,620 --> 00:02:54,257
There's been a huge increase
in monster attacks, too.

32
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,877
They're controlled by the Netherlord.

33
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:59,257
That's the name of the Demon Lord's
nefarious left-armed general.

34
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:01,877
Goodness, I had no idea
it was that serious.

35
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:02,940
What a shock!

36
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:05,597
Though I shouldn't be surprised
that info hadn't reached me when

37
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:09,157
everyone knows I'm the least capable
out of all the Stratum directors.

38
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:11,600
I'm definitely not cut out for this job.

39
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:12,940
This poor director.

40
00:03:13,420 --> 00:03:15,200
She has zero confidence.

41
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:18,620
We're saved!

42
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:20,160
His food is delicious!

43
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:22,520
I'm so thankful! Excellent.

44
00:03:22,820 --> 00:03:24,879
Everyone seems happy with the food.

45
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:29,317
I checked for a magic stone at the item
shop, but it seems they're out of stock.

46
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,341
That's not good.

47
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:33,877
Well, we aren't going anywhere as long
as the transfer circle won't work.

48
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:36,548
I have an idea for how
to get a magic stone.

49
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:41,581
In the meantime, could you adjust the
transfer circle and see if that helps matters?

50
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,540
I'll try, but no promises.

51
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:46,760
You're a co-in there?

52
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:49,540
No, he's one step ahead, huh, Boxo?

53
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:52,211
Yes, I plan to venture into the labyrinth.

54
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,280
Huh? What's that?

55
00:03:56,480 --> 00:03:58,680
Duh-er-axe t-er-la-insane!

56
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:01,313
Maybe some hunters survived the attacks.

57
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:03,960
Then we have no time to waste.

58
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,400
Thanks, Boxer.

59
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:07,382
That's helpful.

60
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:11,750
Don't worry.

61
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:12,670
We've got you.

62
00:04:12,753 --> 00:04:14,540
Oh, thank you so very much.

63
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:16,390
Much?

64
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:19,050
Yep.

65
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:21,237
Seems like a normal
reaction to the sight of

66
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:23,908
a bear carrying a
cardboard vending machine.

67
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:25,880
Oh, this one is with me.

68
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:27,700
And, um, that one too.

69
00:04:31,220 --> 00:04:33,537
Goodness, did that box just change shape?

70
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:35,877
The details can wait,
but for the time being,

71
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:38,877
you should think of our friend
as a special magic item.

72
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:39,790
Amazing.

73
00:04:39,873 --> 00:04:42,520
Nice to meet you, magic item. Hello there.

74
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:45,280
Wow, the magic item responded.

75
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:49,762
As for the monsters, you may leave
it to these two to defeat them.

76
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:54,329
Everyone, cover your ears!

77
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:05,377
Something tells me they could have
handled this just fine without our help.

78
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:09,957
Wow, I've never heard of an Unasusu and
a Curacao that could overwhelm monsters.

79
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:12,057
These two are unique among their kind.

80
00:05:12,140 --> 00:05:14,077
They're outstanding and very friendly.

81
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:16,657
And a certain someone's
power made them stronger.

82
00:05:16,740 --> 00:05:18,377
A certain someone's power?

83
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:19,720
Color me curious.

84
00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:22,804
I will clean up this mess,
so please be patient.

85
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:25,366
What's that dirt ball thingy?

86
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:32,987
I have to ask, what is
that dirt ball thingy?

87
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:35,217
I'll explain, but first things first.

88
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:38,537
Would it be an imposition if I
asked who the two of you might be?

89
00:05:38,620 --> 00:05:39,780
Pardon my rudeness.

90
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:44,197
I'm Director Bear, head of the Hunter's
Association on Clearflow Lake Stratum.

91
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:48,737
This here is Boxxo, and he's a magic item
with the mind and soul of a human being.

92
00:05:48,820 --> 00:05:52,537
He's fully sentient and a dependable
ally, someone you can talk to.

93
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:53,450
Hello there!

94
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:56,820
A human consciousness
contained within a magic item?

95
00:05:57,220 --> 00:05:59,808
Wow, that's a bit like
that certain someone.

96
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:02,200
Who could she be talking about?

97
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:05,797
Now please allow me to
introduce myself and my friends.

98
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:06,800
I am Kikuyu.

99
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:10,680
The white in Asusu is Botan,
the black here is Kuroyata.

100
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:16,896
Based on what I saw of that battle,
these two are exceptionally strong.

101
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:20,297
Makes me wonder if the girl
has any power of her own?

102
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:24,177
My powers are the ability to
control a tiny amount of cold air.

103
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:27,277
And the ability to move
while concealing my presence.

104
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,190
Huh,

105
00:06:28,273 --> 00:06:29,797
if she can mask her presence,

106
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:32,277
she could just hide while the
others handle all the combat!

107
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:33,837
Yes, that is true.

108
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:37,257
I am always relying on
Kuroyata and Botan to save me.

109
00:06:37,340 --> 00:06:40,240
I guess that makes her an animal handler?

110
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:42,680
Oh no, I am not an animal handler.

111
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:46,797
They are smart enough to think on their
own and comprehend complex situations.

112
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:49,704
I am simply their friend
who benefits from that.

113
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:53,597
Kikuyu, would it be uncouth of me
to ask whom you're speaking with?

114
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:54,920
With me, that's who.

115
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,720
Oh, wait a minute.

116
00:06:56,980 --> 00:06:59,617
Was she answering me even
though I wasn't vocalizing?

117
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:04,017
Why, I can hear the inner voice of any
material being that I am able to touch.

118
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:05,000
Whoa, for real?

119
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:07,200
Yes, for real.

120
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:11,477
Oh, but it was rude of me to do
that without asking permission.

121
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:13,780
I'm sorry. Ease! Okay!

122
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:18,277
Um, if you're hungry, we can have a
quick snack while we get acquainted.

123
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,620
Sure, let's do that.

124
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:21,437
Mealtime means it's my time, baby.

125
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:22,350
Good.

126
00:07:22,433 --> 00:07:25,806
Then as thanks, I shall provide
the food for our little repass.

127
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:28,390
Huh?

128
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:32,245
She's not about to grow a plant
for us to eat right now, is she?

129
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:34,730
Whoa!

130
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,350
What?

131
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:39,246
How in the world does
that strange magic work?

132
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:41,857
Not only does this piece
of field absorb monsters?

133
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:44,077
and transform their bodies into nutrients!

134
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:49,440
but if you plant and water a seedling,
my friend can make it grow rapidly!

135
00:07:50,380 --> 00:07:53,100
Did she call the dirt
ball a piece of field?

136
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:01,299
It will be a short while
before it finishes cooking,

137
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:04,637
so I will tell you a little
more about us in the meantime.

138
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:08,717
I must preface by saying that you might
find this story difficult to believe,

139
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:09,920
but it is all true.

140
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:14,560
And so, this is the story
of a very kind field.

141
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:19,580
Once upon a time, there was an old
woman living in a remote village.

142
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,765
Then one day, out of the blue,

143
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:24,277
she found that there was a
soul dwelling in her field.

144
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:28,177
It was a person who had come from
another world and turned into a field.

145
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:32,940
He couldn't speak to her, but every
day, the old woman cultivated him. Huh?

146
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:34,800
A soul inhabiting a field?

147
00:08:34,940 --> 00:08:35,897
That's pretty weird.

148
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:39,157
Well, I guess a soul inside a
vending machine has no room to talk.

149
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:42,957
Also, since it came from another world,
our circumstances are very similar.

150
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:47,320
One day, the old woman passed away,
and the field was left all alone.

151
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:51,757
However, even a field like him had
managed to make some animal friends.

152
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:54,520
By animal, does she
mean Kuroyata and Botan?

153
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:57,037
He spent many quiet days with the animals,

154
00:08:57,120 --> 00:09:00,697
until one day, a girl came
along, fleeing from something.

155
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:04,380
The field took pity on her and
rescued her from her pursuers.

156
00:09:04,660 --> 00:09:08,597
The field wanted to save even more
people, and it went on a journey,

157
00:09:08,680 --> 00:09:11,137
eventually arriving at a
fortified city in the north.

158
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:13,197
This might sound odd coming
from a vending machine,

159
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:16,337
but a field going on a journey
sounds too far-fetched even for me.

160
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:18,017
There was a fierce battle going on there

161
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:20,297
between the citizens and
the Demon Lord's forces.

162
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:23,737
The field saw it as an opportunity
and threw himself into the fight.

163
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:25,077
Despite being a field.

164
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:27,777
The field managed to drive
back the Demon Lord's forces,

165
00:09:27,860 --> 00:09:30,997
earning a temporary time of
peace for the fortified city.

166
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:32,580
This field kicks ass.

167
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:35,737
Then he marched into the Demon Lord's
stronghold and fought fiercely,

168
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:37,337
allowing his friends to flee.

169
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:41,217
Once his friends had escaped, the
field shut down his consciousness.

170
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:44,577
If this story were about a hero,
I might be really inspired by it.

171
00:09:44,660 --> 00:09:46,660
But the main character is a field.

172
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:50,717
Anyway, given how Kiku, you called
that thing the piece of field,

173
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:53,937
I can safely assume she and the
animals were the friends who got away.

174
00:09:54,020 --> 00:09:56,660
We wanted to go see Field in his entirety,

175
00:09:57,060 --> 00:10:00,057
but we couldn't make it past the
huge wall that's blocking the

176
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:03,377
road leading from the fortified
city to the Demon Lord's domain.

177
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:06,097
And then we heard a rumor we
thought could be of use to us,

178
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:10,004
that the Demon Lord's left-armed
general is here in this dungeon.

179
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:12,997
That information is what
led us to this stratum,

180
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:15,198
and that about catches us up to now.

181
00:10:16,940 --> 00:10:18,840
Voxo! Voxo! Voxo?

182
00:10:20,740 --> 00:10:22,440
So, that's the situation.

183
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:24,280
Yes, I understand.

184
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:27,437
Which means that even if I manage
to meet with the Netherlord,

185
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:30,857
it's still unlikely that I could
get him to tell me the way.

186
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:33,800
Oh, these are ready to eat! Here you go!

187
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:35,300
Thank you very much!

188
00:10:39,140 --> 00:10:41,552
Oh, this is delicious, moist, and fluffy!

189
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:43,897
It's an explosion of
sweetness in my mouth!

190
00:10:43,980 --> 00:10:46,300
I'm so delighted that you enjoy it!

191
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:48,877
But this isn't even
one-tenth as good as the

192
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:50,977
vegetables I used to
harvest from Field himself!

193
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:54,060
And one-tenth is even a
little too high, I thought.

194
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:56,397
Vegetables ten times better than that?

195
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:57,310
Impressive.

196
00:10:57,393 --> 00:10:59,117
Oh, hey, they've got nothing to drink.

197
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:01,797
This will go well with
roasted sweet potatoes.

198
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:03,697
Oh my, what are those floating things?

199
00:11:03,780 --> 00:11:06,357
Just wait, Boxo produced
some drinks for us.

200
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:08,600
All you do is open the lid like so.

201
00:11:11,980 --> 00:11:14,000
Wow, it's so cold and tasty.

202
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:17,027
So Boxo has the ability
to serve cold drinks?

203
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:18,817
Oh, much more than just that.

204
00:11:18,900 --> 00:11:21,157
He provides food and all
kinds of other goods.

205
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:23,820
He's a dependable guy, that Boxo. Oh, yes.

206
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:27,017
Field was able to produce any kind
of vegetable you could think of.

207
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:29,837
Boxo sounds surprisingly
similar to him after all.

208
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:30,750
Oh, right.

209
00:11:30,833 --> 00:11:33,465
There's something I really
want to tell Kikuyu.

210
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:40,280
Did you say that you also came
here from another world? Yes.

211
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:45,769
It would seem the soul inside Boxo is
not of our world, just like your field.

212
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:46,850
I see.

213
00:11:46,933 --> 00:11:49,997
Then I wonder if he might even have
come from the same place his field did.

214
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,997
If we manage to make our way to him,

215
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:54,197
you should try talking
to him about such things.

216
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,600
I'd love nothing more.

217
00:11:55,860 --> 00:12:00,137
If he's Japanese like me, then I'll have
all kinds of things to discuss with him.

218
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:01,050
Yes!

219
00:12:03,740 --> 00:12:06,916
We've joined forces and are
traveling with Kikuyu now.

220
00:12:07,340 --> 00:12:09,575
Which means I get to ride in the cart.

221
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,800
It's getting darker by the second.

222
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:19,953
I think it would be wise if
we camped here for the night.

223
00:12:23,460 --> 00:12:24,877
And what are these things?

224
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:26,019
They're delicious.

225
00:12:27,860 --> 00:12:30,036
And these other round things are too.

226
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:33,377
I'm glad she seems to like the food,
but it's time to seal the deal.

227
00:12:33,460 --> 00:12:36,917
And I know the way to a lady's
heart is through her taste buds.

228
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:37,860
Form change!

229
00:12:41,820 --> 00:12:43,780
Wow, a whole new set of items?

230
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:45,197
Some eaters.

231
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:47,600
I've never seen so many sweets before!

232
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:52,010
Amazing!

233
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:55,057
This texture is completely
new to me, and I love it!

234
00:12:55,140 --> 00:12:56,316
Let's try this next.

235
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:01,330
Delicious!

236
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:03,880
Though I must say,

237
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:06,317
this would be even more
outrageously delicious if

238
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:08,597
it had been made with the
fruit that field had grown.

239
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:10,856
Yeah, I'd like to sample that myself.

240
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:15,060
Uh, I'm sorry, but might I trouble
you for something to eat, too?

241
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:16,340
My bad, Director!

242
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:17,816
I completely forgot!

243
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:27,120
So, Boxo, what do you think of Kikuyu?

244
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:29,860
Ice-ca-ed. Agreed.

245
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,057
She's considerate and very smart, too.

246
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:35,077
So much so that her mind and
appearance don't seem to match.

247
00:13:35,160 --> 00:13:36,042
He has a point.

248
00:13:36,180 --> 00:13:38,937
You rarely see children her age
who have such strong character.

249
00:13:39,020 --> 00:13:40,549
In fact, they don't exist.

250
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:45,197
Now that I think about it, it seems
unlikely that Kikuyu is a human child.

251
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:48,457
Based on her looks and abilities,
she must be some other race.

252
00:13:48,540 --> 00:13:49,920
Probably a snow child.

253
00:13:50,180 --> 00:13:51,380
A snow child?

254
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:54,397
I've heard that until a
snow child becomes an adult,

255
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:56,937
they retain the form of
a six-year-old child.

256
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:59,837
So their appearance doesn't
match their true age.

257
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:02,297
The snow children have
very special powers.

258
00:14:02,380 --> 00:14:06,577
For that reason, they're a highly targeted
race and they're in danger of extinction.

259
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:10,317
In fact, until we met Kikuyu, I
thought they were already extinct.

260
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:12,753
Special powers that everyone goes after?

261
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:18,277
Legend has it that if you behead a snow
child on the day it becomes an adult,

262
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:21,697
they will transform into a magical
ice statue that will never melt.

263
00:14:21,780 --> 00:14:23,077
As for the severed head,

264
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:25,457
it will continue to utter
curses that have the power

265
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:28,364
to contaminate entire
regions in one fell swoop.

266
00:14:28,820 --> 00:14:31,717
I hear there are whole
nations that perish that way.

267
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:35,577
That's a killer power, but what it
takes to invoke it is too cruel.

268
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:39,189
Beheading someone to cast a
curse is a horrible thing to do.

269
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:41,478
And that's not the end of it either.

270
00:14:41,980 --> 00:14:45,857
The Headless Ice Statue becomes a
sort of catch-all curse remover.

271
00:14:45,940 --> 00:14:50,352
Just place it next to a cursed person,
and it will cleanse them of any hex.

272
00:14:50,580 --> 00:14:51,980
It removes curses?

273
00:14:52,220 --> 00:14:53,317
That means...

274
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:54,740
Co-A-P-A-T-E!

275
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:58,857
I have no doubt that it could
dispel Kerry Oil's son's affliction.

276
00:14:58,940 --> 00:15:01,837
Oh man, if the Captain knew about this...

277
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:05,397
Which is why we mustn't utter
this knowledge to a solitary soul.

278
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:07,245
The secret must remain hidden.

279
00:15:07,620 --> 00:15:08,450
Yes!

280
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:12,580
No matter what happens, we can't
let this girl end up a victim.

281
00:15:20,140 --> 00:15:21,537
Oh, that's a...

282
00:15:21,620 --> 00:15:22,940
A magic stone.

283
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:27,317
But I don't know if it's powerful enough
to get the transfer circle up and running.

284
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:28,400
Oh, that's right.

285
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:32,297
Without Hulemy, we don't know how much
power we need from the magic stones.

286
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:35,615
We'd better rendezvous with
Hulemy and see what's what.

287
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:41,135
Seems it can't pass through after all.

288
00:15:41,220 --> 00:15:43,044
I already tried it once before,

289
00:15:43,220 --> 00:15:46,257
but I don't believe there's any way
to get this piece of field through.

290
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:48,917
I heard this barrier can
detect monster wavelengths

291
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,197
and prevent the passage of those energies.

292
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:53,997
I'll bet the piece of
field-absorbed monsters soaked up

293
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:56,717
their wavelengths and the barrier
can't tell the difference.

294
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:58,271
I guess that makes sense.

295
00:15:58,460 --> 00:16:03,107
But I can't leave field behind here
without worrying something bad will happen.

296
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:05,967
There's still one thing
that I'd like to try.

297
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:09,760
All right, Kikoyu, try to cross now.

298
00:16:13,260 --> 00:16:15,000
Thank goodness! It worked!

299
00:16:15,420 --> 00:16:18,977
So Bokso's barrier can successfully
interrupt the labyrinth barrier,

300
00:16:19,060 --> 00:16:19,957
that's good to know.

301
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:23,397
Well, nice to meet you on this
side, Kikoyu, Kuroyata, and Botan.

302
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:24,340
Yes, Hulemy.

303
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:26,060
We thank you very much.

304
00:16:28,440 --> 00:16:29,911
We're back to square one.

305
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:33,397
But we made some dependable friends,
and that's always a good thing.

306
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:34,700
Director Bear,

307
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:39,337
I finished adjusting the transfer circle
so I can accompany you all next time.

308
00:16:39,420 --> 00:16:40,250
Oh, good.

309
00:16:40,333 --> 00:16:41,277
You'll be most welcome.

310
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:42,190
Hello there!

311
00:16:44,360 --> 00:16:46,066
We spent the night at an inn.

312
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:49,645
Then we ventured into
the labyrinth once again.

313
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:51,620
After much discussion,

314
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:55,737
we arrived at the conclusion that rather
than do an exhaustive search for stones,

315
00:16:55,820 --> 00:16:59,697
we should try to defeat the dangerous Lava
Fiend monster and get its magic stone.

316
00:16:59,780 --> 00:17:01,240
That lava fiend?

317
00:17:01,620 --> 00:17:03,817
Well, it's more dangerous
than a stratum lord!

318
00:17:03,900 --> 00:17:06,177
But both Hulemy and Director
Bear thought we'd be fine.

319
00:17:06,260 --> 00:17:07,966
with such a formidable party.

320
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:11,777
Then shall I have Kuroyata fly above
the maze and seek out the lava fiend?

321
00:17:11,860 --> 00:17:13,077
If you wouldn't mind.

322
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:13,990
Right.

323
00:17:14,260 --> 00:17:16,025
Kuroyata, please do as I said!

324
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:19,150
Hmm.

325
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:21,337
We might as well end the search for today.

326
00:17:21,420 --> 00:17:23,960
Let's start setting up camp. Good call.

327
00:17:24,180 --> 00:17:26,977
So are you two gonna duke it out to
see who gets to make dinner tonight?

328
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:31,097
Voxo was in charge yesterday, so it
seems only fair that I do it tonight.

329
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:32,880
I could add da oo-it.

330
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:34,925
Oh no, you take it easy today.

331
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,857
Fresh vegetables are good for your skin,

332
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:39,417
and they also help prevent
all kinds of diseases.

333
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,340
I da oo-s will eat still.

334
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:42,872
Did you just say sweets?

335
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:46,817
Apparently, Hulemy craves sweets
after she's had a strenuous think.

336
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:50,317
And her favorite guilty pleasure
foods are all full of sugar.

337
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:51,230
Hmm.

338
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:55,852
Director Bear sounds non-committal,
but I know what my regulars' faves are.

339
00:17:57,740 --> 00:17:59,537
Bear's gotta have their salmon.

340
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:02,973
Let's see if he can resist
this veritable salmon torrent.

341
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:04,657
Oh, dang, what's that?

342
00:18:04,740 --> 00:18:08,337
I mean, why don't we just go with
Boxo's goods for this evening's meal?

343
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,250
Yes, let's.

344
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:10,640
No objections from me.

345
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:12,460
Hey, no fair, Boxo.

346
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:15,160
I look forward to serving you again.

347
00:18:15,940 --> 00:18:16,770
Really?

348
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:23,097
With the sweet taste of
yesterday's victory still fresh,

349
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:25,827
I got some sleep last
night, a rarity for me.

350
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:29,017
Kikuyu stood watch from late
night until early morning,

351
00:18:29,100 --> 00:18:30,924
so I was able to sleep soundly.

352
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:34,637
Now, I'd better start making
breakfast for everyone.

353
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:35,838
Good morning, Boxo!

354
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:39,577
I made some soup that's loaded with
vegetables, and it's very good for you!

355
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:40,490
She got me!

356
00:18:40,573 --> 00:18:42,980
This was her secret plan all along!

357
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:46,100
Wow, so savory!

358
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:49,419
The flavor is amazing, and
it's so restorative, too!

359
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,294
Welcome back, Kariata!

360
00:18:53,560 --> 00:18:54,840
Okay, thank you.

361
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:58,049
It seems Kuroyata has
found the Lava Fiend.

362
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:00,100
Since we know where it is,

363
00:19:00,260 --> 00:19:03,848
I can share my strategy for
defeating it before we get there.

364
00:19:05,180 --> 00:19:08,560
It should be somewhere around here. Oh!

365
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:13,000
There it goes now.

366
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:19,980
And that's a wall I built
using giant concrete slabs.

367
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:21,677
But I didn't stop there.

368
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:22,920
I built two walls.

369
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,494
Now why did I do such a thing, you ask?

370
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:27,580
That's why.

371
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,500
Have fun in your icy bath, Lava Fiend.

372
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:35,000
No heat stands a chance against
that much ice water, not even yours.

373
00:19:35,840 --> 00:19:40,252
Though it might have only hardened your
outside, that's good enough for us.

374
00:19:42,380 --> 00:19:46,086
According to Hulemy, the Lava
Fiend's weak point is its throat.

375
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,820
You might win an extra item!

376
00:19:56,720 --> 00:19:59,160
I look forward to your next use.

377
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:02,910
Huh?

378
00:20:03,060 --> 00:20:04,040
It regenerated?

379
00:20:04,260 --> 00:20:05,260
That ain't good!

380
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:07,520
Whoa! What now?

381
00:20:11,760 --> 00:20:14,500
Wait, could it be... no way!

382
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:16,160
A stratum split?

383
00:20:16,460 --> 00:20:17,897
And isn't that...

384
00:20:17,980 --> 00:20:19,020
Lamas?

385
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:21,220
How typical.

386
00:20:21,380 --> 00:20:24,557
That doofus must have helped
herself to my inventions again.

387
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:25,470
Boxxo!

388
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:29,710
Boxxo!

389
00:20:29,793 --> 00:20:30,915
I'm glad you're okay!

390
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:33,280
Hold on, who's this bird guy? End!

391
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:36,080
I found you!

392
00:20:36,220 --> 00:20:38,060
We're together again! Bad!

393
00:20:38,560 --> 00:20:40,280
Wait, are you mad at me?

394
00:20:41,460 --> 00:20:42,290
Yes!

395
00:20:42,373 --> 00:20:43,203
You're evil!

396
00:20:43,286 --> 00:20:44,116
What?

397
00:20:44,199 --> 00:20:46,160
No, Boxxo, please don't be mad!

398
00:20:46,460 --> 00:20:47,519
That was reckless.

399
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:49,477
You could have died if
something went wrong.

400
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:52,337
If you've got an explanation,
we would like to hear it, too.

401
00:20:52,420 --> 00:20:55,797
Man, shouldn't this be the part
where we're happy to see each other?

402
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:56,800
Talk, Lamas.

403
00:20:56,960 --> 00:21:01,157
Tell us what happened since we last saw
you and how you came to fall from the sky.

404
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:03,897
Well, you see, right
after I last saw you guys,

405
00:21:03,980 --> 00:21:07,797
Director Origin and I were lucky enough to
transfer to the Clear Flow Lake stratum.

406
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:09,897
Then I remembered how
Director Bear said if you hit

407
00:21:09,980 --> 00:21:12,617
a stratum split real hard
at exactly the right spot,

408
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:14,297
you might be able to make it split again.

409
00:21:14,380 --> 00:21:16,917
And then Hulami's magic item
that lets you safely drop

410
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:19,237
from high up and the one
that freezes water were just,

411
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:20,150
like, right there.

412
00:21:20,233 --> 00:21:22,217
And Hulemy wasn't around
to ask, so I used him.

413
00:21:22,300 --> 00:21:23,130
I'm sorry.

414
00:21:23,213 --> 00:21:25,797
And so I kind of punched the
frozen pond with all my might.

415
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:27,137
And then the stratum split again.

416
00:21:27,220 --> 00:21:29,517
and I just sort of tumbled
down into the crack.

417
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:31,240
Well, here I am.

418
00:21:32,540 --> 00:21:35,011
Those deep sighs are definitely warranted.

419
00:21:35,320 --> 00:21:36,908
That was all too impulsive.

420
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:40,617
But Lamas, what if we hadn't
been in the labyrinth stratum?

421
00:21:40,700 --> 00:21:42,171
What would you have done?

422
00:21:42,440 --> 00:21:44,240
Well, uh, I don't know.

423
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:45,737
I had a feeling you were here.

424
00:21:45,820 --> 00:21:47,377
That's quite the leap of faith!

425
00:21:47,460 --> 00:21:49,997
The most important thing
is that you're safe, Lamas.

426
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:51,977
But I want you to realize we're all angry

427
00:21:52,060 --> 00:21:55,001
because we care about you
and what happens to you.

428
00:21:55,260 --> 00:21:58,320
Yeah, I'm sorry if I had you guys worried.

429
00:21:58,700 --> 00:22:00,857
Well, we're together
and that's what matters.

430
00:22:00,940 --> 00:22:01,770
You're safe.

431
00:22:02,300 --> 00:22:04,420
Yeah, Hulemy, I am back!

432
00:22:17,460 --> 00:22:25,420
. . .

433
00:22:55,420 --> 00:22:59,420
No memory, the words of
the way over the world?

434
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:04,220
I'll move on to the same time!

435
00:23:05,140 --> 00:23:06,657
I'll keep my own love.

436
00:23:06,740 --> 00:23:07,570
I'll keep my own memory.

437
00:23:07,653 --> 00:23:11,080
As I can't wait for my own time!

438
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:15,400
I'll keep my own love.

439
00:23:17,420 --> 00:23:22,380
I'll keep my own love.

440
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:36,780
You could even win a reward!

441
00:23:37,820 --> 00:23:39,938
I look forward to serving you again!
